-- title:
--   Hilbert's Theorem 90 for a free cyclic action
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a commutative ring that is Artinian and reduced, and let $\theta : E \to E$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $k$ be a natural number with $k > 0$ such that the $k$-fold iterate $\theta^{[k]}$ is the identity on $E$, i.e. $\theta^{[k]}(x) = x$ for all $x \in E$ (so $\theta$ is in particular bijective, of order dividing $k$). Assume the action of $\theta$ is free in the following sense: for every idempotent $e \in E$ with $e \neq 0$ and every natural number $i$ with $0 < i < k$, it is not the case that $\theta^{[i]}(e x) = e x$ for all $x \in E$; that is, $\theta^{[i]}$ fails to act as the identity on the ideal $eE$. Then for every unit $c \in E^{\times}$ whose twisted norm is trivial, meaning that the product of the list $\bigl(\theta^{[i]}(c)\bigr)_{i = 0}^{k-1}$, taken in increasing order of $i$, equals $1$ in $E$, there exists a unit $z \in E^{\times}$ with $z = c \cdot \theta(z)$ as elements of $E$.
--
--   This is the multiplicative Hilbert Theorem 90 for the cyclic group generated by $\theta$ acting freely on a reduced Artinian ring, i.e. on a finite product of fields: units of twisted norm one are coboundaries. It is used in the analysis of twisted conjugacy in centraliser algebras of regular semisimple elements, via [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isCompact_setOf_mem_centralizer_normString_twistedConj_mem_subset_twistedCentralizer_mul_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isCompact_setOf_mem_centralizer_normString_twistedConj_mem_subset_twistedCentralizer_mul_of_isArtinianRing).
